# 2026 SEO Master Rules (Strict Compliance)

## 1. Anti-Thin Content Rule
- **Minimum Word Count:** Every generated page MUST contain at least 300 words of unique, non-repetitive, high-value technical text.
- **No Generic Slop:** Do not use identical "how-to" templates. The AI must vary the technical advice based on the specific Provider (Google, Outlook, etc.) and Registrar (GoDaddy, Cloudflare, etc.).
- **Functional Value:** Every page must include a "One-Minute Fix" code block or a DNS validator component to ensure it is a "Utility" and not just a "Gateway" page.

## 2. Gateway/Doorway Penalty Avoidance
- **Natural Language H1s:** NO keyword fragments (e.g., "SPF Gmail Fix"). Use: "How to Resolve SPF Record Alignment Issues for Gmail on Cloudflare (2026 Guide)".
- **Browsable Hierarchy:** Every page must be part of a hub-and-spoke system. It must link back to its Topic Hub (SPF, DKIM, or DMARC) and 2-3 "Related Fixes."
- **Internal Linking:** Zero "Island Pages." Every page must be accessible via the main site navigation or a hub page.

## 3. Authority & Trust (Exposure Ninja Style)
- **First-Party Experience:** Use expert language: "Our technical audit shows..." or "In 2026, Google and Yahoo's new sender requirements state...".
- **Psychographic Targeting:** Address the "Panicked Founder" (clear solution at the top) and the "IT Admin" (deep technical details below) on every page.